# Apparition release signers, in ssh-keygen allowed_signers format.
#
# Every Apparition release is one SHA256SUMS file listing its assets, signed with
# `ssh-keygen -Y sign -n apparition-release` (SSHSIG). The installer and the app verify a
# download against these keys before using it, and refuse anything the signature doesn't
# cover. Download URLs are not trusted at all: an asset can come from any host as long as
# its hash is in a signed manifest.
#
# TWO KEYS, both pinned from the first release that ships this file: the everyday YubiKey
# (needs a PIN and a touch, never on disk or in CI) and an offline backup, for when the
# YubiKey is lost or broken. A backup added later would be worthless: nothing already
# installed would trust it, and the release introducing it couldn't be verified.
#
# They are the same two keys that sign Longwave releases and the illixion.github.io
# ssh-keys-updater manifests, so there is one pair to protect. The namespace differs
# ("apparition-release", not "file"), so a signature made for those can't pass as an
# Apparition release.
#
# The release site (apparition.illixion.com, scripts/publish.py) keeps a copy and checks it
# matches this one.
